{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>הלא.</b> An opening [particle], like התר:" "<b>חרצובות.</b> Like קשרים (bonds), and similarly כי אין חרצובות למותם (Psalms 73:4):" "<b>מוטה.</b> Like מטת עלכם (Leviticus 26:13). The meaning is to free the slaves, as written in the book of Jeremiah [34]:" "(העשוקים משפט). <b>רצוצים.</b> (Like רצוצים) — these are the oppressed slaves, like רצוץ משפט (Hosea 5:11), like ואת מי רצותי (1 Samuel 12:3). Some say that חרצובות רשע refers to thoughts, but the first [interpretation] is correct in my eyes."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:08.219541423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}